From: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH v3 24/24] dmaengine: sdxi: add COMPRESS/DECOMPRESS descriptors and userspace char device

This patch extends the SDXI driver (introduced in the preceding v3
series) with two capabilities that are intentionally omitted from the
upstream submission but are required for local emulator-based testing:

  1. COMPRESS / DECOMPRESS DMAB subtypes (0x04 / 0x05).
  2. A /dev/sdxi<N> char device that exposes copy, compress, and
     decompress operations to userspace via ioctl.

Background
----------
The upstream v3 patchset covers COPY/NOP/SYNC/INTR descriptors.
Compression support requires a hardware accelerator block that is not
present on all SDXI implementations; it is therefore deferred from the
mainline submission.  This patch documents the ABI so that the vfio-user
emulator (rocm-sdxi) and future hardware can share a common interface.

COMPRESS / DECOMPRESS descriptor layout (DMAB, 64 bytes)
---------------------------------------------------------
The same 64-byte descriptor format used for COPY applies:

  Offset  Size  Field
  0       4     opcode: VL=1, SUBTYPE=0x04 (COMPRESS) or 0x05 (DECOMPRESS), TYPE=0x001 (DMAB)
  4       4     src_len:  number of bytes to compress/decompress
  8       4     dst_cap:  capacity of destination buffer in bytes
  12      4     level:    compression level (0=default, 1-9=zlib; ignored for DECOMPRESS)
  16      8     src_addr: source GPA (input data)
  24      8     dst_addr: destination GPA (output data)
  32      24    reserved
  56      8     csb_ptr:  GPA of 32-byte CSB (struct sdxi_cst_blk)

The CSB result_len field (bytes 12-19 of struct sdxi_cst_blk) contains
the number of bytes written to dst_addr on successful completion.

New constants in <linux/dma/sdxi.h>
------------------------------------
  SDXI_DSC_OP_SUBTYPE_COMPRESS    0x04U
  SDXI_DSC_OP_SUBTYPE_DECOMPRESS  0x05U

Char device (drivers/dma/sdxi/sdxi_char.c)
-------------------------------------------
Registered as a misc device (/dev/sdxi<devfn>).  It is built as part of
sdxi.ko and uses the driver's internal context-management APIs rather
than opening PCI resources directly.

UAPI header (include/uapi/linux/sdxi_user.h)
--------------------------------------------
Shared between the kernel module and userspace.  Three ioctl structures:

  struct sdxi_ioc_memcpy      SDXI_IOC_MEMCPY     _IOW ('X', 1, ...)
  struct sdxi_ioc_compress    SDXI_IOC_COMPRESS    _IOWR('X', 2, ...)
  struct sdxi_ioc_decompress  SDXI_IOC_DECOMPRESS  _IOWR('X', 3, ...)

For compress and decompress the ioctl writes back the actual output
length in the out_len field of the struct before returning.

NOTE: This patch targets the out-of-tree emulator driver (sdxi_char.c
in drivers/sdxi_char/).  The in-tree version would integrate with
sdxi.ko using the driver-internal context APIs and live under
drivers/dma/sdxi/ instead.

Signed-off-by: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
